 #:seon.task{:name "a-send-inside-a-do-form-leaves-a-message"
             :intent "`seon.cluster.turn-test/a-turn-delivers-what-a-form-asks-to-send-and-still-finishes` finds `message-tx` nil on HEAD (measured by bin/seon check at HEAD with long tests, run 637bbb669483 on df21007f0 (`docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-13/turn-reds-triage.md#measured-reds-on-head-7f96b6cba-32-vars`)): a `my.message/send` evaluated inside a `do` form recorded no `:seon.message/id` fact, though the turn still finished. Reproduce with one form `(do (my.message/send ...) 1)` through the one eval path on a branch, then read `seon.cluster.message/send-call` and `seon.cluster.message/send!` for where the send is staged (a send is an effect of its evaluation, recorded in the same transaction as the evaluation) and fix the producer that drops it. Done when the test is green."}
